      "care": "Protect shoots from frost. Earth up or mulch to keep tubers covered. Weed carefully. Water as tubers swell, especially in pots.",
      "methods": [
        {
          "title": "Chit",
          "text": "Stand certified seed potatoes with their eyes upwards in a cool, light, frost-free place to sprout. Chitting is most useful for first earlies."
        },
        {
          "title": "Plant in the ground",
          "text": "Early crops need a mild or protected spot. Dig a trench or holes about 6 in. deep. Set tubers on the bottom, sprouts up. Cover gently and water well."
        },
        {
          "title": "Under mulch",
          "text": "Lay tubers on the soil. Cover thickly with mulch to exclude light. Top up as they grow and check for slugs."
        },
        {
          "title": "In containers",
          "text": "Use a large pot with drainage holes. Set tubers on a shallow layer of compost. Cover and top up as the stems grow."
        }
      ],
